Reset the completed WaveOut source queue before MCI closes the movie.

Wine 10 WOD_PushData stops and resets its client once the completed header
queue is empty. The ALSA client reset drops, resets and prepares its PCM.
Actual original intro output records this transition independently of the
later MCI reset/close, discarding the initial post-source lead-in period.
The native producer previously only recovered underruns until MCI closed.

After the source drains, reset its queue once after that first driver
lead-in, latch completion, then retain period-sized stopped-client silence.
No source bytes or timestamps are shifted or fitted. Original whole-output
and shared-clock parity remain separate requirements.

